1281 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 385 0 R/E(No representation is made that these goals or objectives will be achieved, in whole or in part, by the Fund. This material is as of the date indicated, is not complete, is subject to change, and does not contain all material information with respect to the Fund. While all information obtained from this document is believed to be accurate, Cretum Capital, LLC makes no warranty as to completeness or accuracy, nor can it accept responsibility for errors appearing in the document. Cretum Capital, LLC has not independently verified any information and has no obligation to update any information. This information is confidential, is the property of the Investment Manager and Cretum Capital, LLC, is directed only to the recipients and their authorized agents and representatives, and may not be reproduced or distributed to any other person without prior written consent. Any distribution to social media is a willful violation of the confidentiality and regulatory restrictions governing this document. Hedge Fund Risk Disclosures: Hedge funds are privately registered investment partnerships, funds or pools that may invest and trade in different markets, strategies and instruments \(including securities, non-securities and derivatives\) and are not subject to the same regulatory requirements as registered investment vehicles, including mutual funds, which have requirements to provide certain periodic and standardized pricing and valuation information to investors. There are substantial risks in investing in hedge funds. You should carefully consider the following: hedge funds represent speculative investments and involve a high degree of risk. An investor could lose all or a substantial portion of their investment. Investors must have the financial ability, sophistication/experience, and willingness to bear the risks of an investment in a hedge fund. An investment in a hedge fund should be discretionary capital set aside strictly for speculative purposes. An investment in a hedge fund is not suitable or desirable for all investors. Only eligible qualified investors may invest in hedge funds. Hedge fund offering documents are not reviewed or approved by federal and state regulators. Hedge funds may be leveraged \(including highly leveraged\) and a hedge fund's performance can be volatile. An investment in a hedge fund may be illiquid and there may be significant restrictions on transferring interests in a hedge fund. There is no secondary market for an investor's investment in a hedge fund nor is one expected to develop. A hedge fund may use a single advisor or employ a single strategy, which could mean a lack of diversification and higher risk. A hedge fund may involve complex tax structures, which should be carefully reviewed, and may involve structures or strategies that may cause delays in important tax information being sent to investors. A hedge fund's fees and expenses may be substantial, regardless of any positive return, and will offset the hedge fund's trading profits. Hedge funds are not required to provide periodic pricing or valuation information to investors. Hedge funds and their managers/advisors may be subject to various conflicts of interest. The foregoing is not a complete list of the risks and other considerations involved in investing in a hedge fund and is subject to the more complete disclosures contained in a hedge fund's confidential offering documents, which should be carefully reviewed. Directors and employees of Cretum Capital may make personal investments in certain hedge fund products for which Cretum Capital is compensated for introducing potential investors. Any personal investment by a director or employee of Cretum Capital in any hedge fund is not a recommendation or promotion of any specific product.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

